1. A dynamic random access memory (DRAM) device comprising:  

a memory cell array divided into a plurality of bank groups, each bank group including a plurality of memory banks;  

a first bus coupled to the plurality of bank groups and configured to transfer a column command to a selected bank group among the plurality of bank groups;  

a second bus coupled to the plurality of bank groups and configured to transfer a column address to the selected bank group;  

a toggle signal generator configured to generate a toggle signal that changes state in response to receipt of column-access commands;  

a column command transmission unit configured to transmit the column command through the first bus to the selected bank group in response to the toggle signal; and  

a column address transmission unit configured to transmit the column address through the second bus to the selected bank group in response to the toggle signal,  

wherein the column command transmission unit and the column address transmission unit are configured to control transmission timing of the column command and the column address based on the toggle signal to support column access operations to the plurality of bank groups.

1. A memory device comprising:  
   a memory cell array including a plurality of bank groups, each bank group including at least one memory bank;  
   a command/address interface configured to receive column commands and column addresses;  
   first and second command buses coupled to the plurality of bank groups;  
   a toggle signal generation unit configured to generate a toggle signal in response to receipt of the column commands, the toggle signal indicating a selected one of the first and second command buses; and  
   command transmission logic configured to, based on the toggle signal, transmit a read command or a write command corresponding to a received column command, together with a corresponding column address, to the selected one of the first and second command buses for execution by a target bank group among the plurality of bank groups.
